      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__vertex__setters_1gaba1257b95725546dd745e2ce06148d8d" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlSetVertexParams</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLVertex *_Vertex, void *_Params)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlSetVertexParams</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Vertex</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>_Params</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Sets the user-defined <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> of a vertex. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Vertex</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target vertex to update the parameters of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to extra memory used by the vertex. May be NULL.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Vertex is NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise updates the parameters of _Vertex, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>NDXL stores the supplied <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> pointer without copying the associated data or managing its lifetime. The pointed-to memory must remain valid for as long as the vertex uses it.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>This function replaces the vertex&apos;s existing parameter pointer without freeing or otherwise managing the memory it previously referenced. The user remains responsible for managing both the previous and new allocations.</para>
</simplesect>
